---
description: Wire known components and assets in the Inspector with SerializeField. Do not rediscover them at runtime.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Serialized references

A component, prefab, or asset that already exists on the prefab or in the scene is assigned in the Inspector.

Use `[SerializeField]` for that reference. Do not fill it in `Awake`, `OnEnable`, or `Start` with `GetComponent`, `GetComponentInChildren`, `GetComponentInParent`, `Find`, or `FindObjectOfType`.

Runtime lookup is only for an object created during play that cannot be assigned ahead of time.

```csharp
public class CharacterMovement : MonoBehaviour
{
    [SerializeField] Character character;
}
```

Assign `character` on the prefab. Do not add a null fallback that calls `GetComponent`.
